          "title": "Graph Convolutional Networks: Message Passing, Oversmoothing, and Depth-Based Performance Analysis",
          "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24054250",
          "publication_date": "2026-11-08",
          "description": "<p>This work investigates Graph Convolutional Networks (GCNs) from their spectral foundations to their practical behavior under increasing network depth.</p>\n<p>First, the mathematical foundations of graph convolution and message passing are examined, including adjacency matrix construction, self-loop addition, symmetric degree normalization, and the propagation of node features across graph layers.</p>",
